      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSActualRootCommutation"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel base E with canonical volume, including the disclosed rank-zero extension; V is C²; 0<α≤β; both global Hessian bounds; η>0 and βη≤1.",
        "Canonical normalized laws/kernel, onto pullback e, SAME U/T, full and centered roots, exact centering, gap, unit and bounded inverse are conclusions. Conditional actions are per-observable AE. L² is not assumed finite-dimensional.",
        "γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη); the inverse acts only on H_P^0=ker⟨e1,·⟩ with inherited Hilbert structure; the legal endpoint αη=1 is retained.",
        "H_perp is exactly ker P (conditional expectation given Y), while H_P^0 is the zero ν-mean macroscopic space. Their complete Hilbert structures, B_0 and V_0 are internally constructed; no onto-kerP or coisometry assumption is introduced.",
        "The concluded global-input implication quantifies every f∈L²(J) with integral zero. R,conditional centering,constant annihilation,adjoint range and norm decomposition are derived internally. Private statement definitions expand literally to the original sealed propositions and add no premise."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X~μ and Z~N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. These are probability laws. Put mY=comap(snd), H_P=L² classes measurable with respect to mY, P=i∘E[·|Y] and the canonical M:u↦u∘snd. Then H_P=ran(P), P is identity on H_P, and there exists an onto linear isometry e:L²(ν;ℝ)≃H_P with i e=M. There is a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized law is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)); Λ.IsCondKernel S and both Λ marginals equal ν. The same joint reflection F(x,y)=(x,2x−y) gives the involutive selfadjoint isometry U, with Uf=f∘F J-almost everywhere for every f. There is a bounded selfadjoint T on the full real L²(ν), with ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere for each u, and preserved integral. On H_P put A=PUP restricted via i and orthogonal projection, and B=(I_J−P)UPi:H_P→L²(J). Then A=eTe⁻¹ is selfadjoint and contractive, PB=0. There is a bounded positive operator Γ on the real scalar-valued L² space with Γ²=I−T². For the SAME transported Γ_P=eΓe⁻¹, positivity holds and Γ_P²=I_H_P−A²=B*B. There is q∈L²(ν;ℝ) equal to one ν-almost everywhere, with Tq=q and ⟨q,u⟩=∫u dν for every u. Set q_P=e q and H_P^0=ker⟨q_P,·⟩, with its inherited Hilbert structure. Membership is exactly zero ν-mean after e⁻¹. The SAME Γ_P annihilates q_P. Put γ=2√(αη)/(1+αη)>0. There exists Γ_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 equal under inclusion to the restriction of Γ_P, positive with Γ_0−γ I positive. Γ_0 is a unit in the algebra of bounded real operators. There exists a bounded real Inv on this SAME centered space with Inv Γ_0=Γ_0 Inv=I and ‖Inv‖≤1/γ. All probability, normalization, range, root, centering, spectral-gap, unit and inverse facts are internally derived from the original inputs; none is an additional public premise. αη=1 and rank-zero E remain legal. No inverse on full H_P is asserted. Define the actual closed conditional-mean-zero space H_perp=ker P in L²(J;ℝ), with its inherited complete Hilbert structure; this is not merely the globally zero-mean joint space. There exists B_0:H_P^0→H_perp whose inclusion equals B i_0. There exists V_0:H_P^0→H_perp with V_0=B_0 Inv, B_0=V_0 Γ_0, V_0* V_0=I and ‖V_0 f‖=‖f‖ for every f∈H_P^0. All these objects and identities are conclusions from the same original inputs. There exists the canonical bounded residual map R:L²(J;ℝ)→H_perp with i_perp Rg=g−Pg for every joint g. The SAME ambient adjoint satisfies B* g=i_0 B_0* Rg for every joint g; the printed intrinsic block adjoint is recovered on H_perp. For every actual joint f∈L²(J;ℝ) with ∫f dJ=0, there exists f_P∈H_P^0 whose inclusion is E[f|Y]. Put f_perp=Rf and f_V=V_0* f_perp∈the SAME H_P^0. Then B* i_perp f_perp=i_0 Γ_0 f_V=Γ_P i_0 f_V, ‖f‖²=‖f_P‖²+‖f_perp‖² and ‖f_V‖≤‖f_perp‖. The preceding independently reviewed ambient-adjoint Test derives f=i i_0 f_P+i_perp f_perp, B* f=Γ_P i_0 f_V and ‖f_V‖²≤‖f‖²−‖f_P‖². The global zero-mean condition is a quantified input restriction to this concluded implication, not an extra assumption on the potential or an operator certificate. The SAME root commutes with T and its transport commutes with A. The SAME Inv on H_P^0 is selfadjoint. There exists an internally constructed A_0:H_P^0→H_P^0 whose inclusion equals A after inclusion; it is selfadjoint,commutes with Γ_0,satisfies A_0²+Γ_0²=I,and commutes with the SAME Inv. The genuine original-input Test proves K=A_0 Inv selfadjoint and I+K²=Inv². All old ambient-adjoint/global-centered-observable conclusions persist. These are ingredients for sharp B23 and B21;neither estimate/rotation nor full dynamics,expected costs or composition is asserted. Private literal proposition definitions store the complete original statements and add no premise or provider.",
      "formula": "[\\Gamma,T]=[\\Gamma_P,A]=[A_0,\\Gamma_0]=[A_0,\\mathrm{Inv}]=0,\\quad\\mathrm{Inv}^*=\\mathrm{Inv},\\quad I+(A_0\\mathrm{Inv})^2=\\mathrm{Inv}^2.",
      "boundary": "Same-root and actual centered inverse commutation plus B23 coefficient square identity only. Sharp B23 norm estimate/B21 rotation/full energy/H1/dynamics/errors/cost/composition not yet proved. All original finite Hilbert/Borel/C2/both Hessians/positive capped eta callers preserved. D=I+T positivity and all commutations are internally proved, never extra public paper premises.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Retain the exact actual witnesses",
          "text": "Reuse the original-input parent and SAME laws,kernel,operators,roots,inverse,polar and centered geometry;fix their exact spaces.",
          "formula": "\\Gamma_P=e\\Gamma e^{-1},\\quad H_P^0=\\ker\\langle q_P,\\cdot\\rangle,\\quad\\Gamma_0^{-1}=\\mathrm{Inv}.",
          "lean": "  classical\n  unfold actual_same_root_inverse_commutation_statement\n  dsimp only\n  let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n  let J := (μ.prod (stdGaussian E)).map\n    (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2))\n  let ν := J.snd\n  let mY : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := MeasurableSpace.comap Prod.snd (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace E)\n  letI : MeasurableSpace (E × E) := Prod.instMeasurableSpace\n  letI : Fact (mY ≤ (inferInstance : MeasurableSpace (E × E))) := ⟨measurable_snd.comap_le⟩\n  let HP := lpMeas ℝ ℝ mY 2 J\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP := HP.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP := HP.innerProductSpace\n  let P : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    HP.subtypeL ∘L condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ := J) measurable_snd.comap_le\n  have hBase := AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.AmbientAdjointCorrector.actual_ambient_adjoint_centered_decomposition\n    (E:=E) (V:=V) (α:=α) (β:=β) (η:=η) hα hαβ hV hH hη hβη\n  rcases hBase with\n    ⟨hμ,hJ,hν,hRange,hPf,S,hS,hSd,hSc,hSf,hSs,e,he,U,hU,hUi,hUs,\n      T,hTs,hAll,hAeq,hAs,hAn,hPB,Γ,hΓ,hΓSq,hΓP,hΓPSq,hGram,\n      q,hqa,hTq,hq,hCenter,hΓPq,hγ,ΓP0,hΓP0,hPos0,hOrder0,hUnit,\n      Inv,hLeft,hRight,hNormInv,B0,hB0,V0,hVdef,hFactor,hVadj,hVnorm,R,hR,hAmbient,hGlobal⟩\n  let A : HP →L[ℝ] HP := HP.orthogonalProjectionOnto ∘L U.toContinuousLinearMap ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let B : HP →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J :=\n    (((1 : Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Lp ℝ 2 J)-P)*U.toContinuousLinearMap*P) ∘L HP.subtypeL\n  let ΓP : HP →L[ℝ] HP := e.conjStarAlgEquiv Γ\n  let qP : HP := e q\n  let HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup HP0 := HP0.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ HP0 := HP0.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace HP0 := (innerSL ℝ qP).isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  let Hperp := P.ker\n  letI : NormedAddCommGroup Hperp := Hperp.normedAddCommGroup\n  letI : InnerProductSpace ℝ Hperp := Hperp.innerProductSpace\n  letI : CompleteSpace Hperp := P.isClosed_ker.completeSpace_coe\n  change HP0 →L[ℝ] Hperp at B0 V0\n  change HP0 →L[ℝ] HP0 at ΓP0 Inv\n  change Lp ℝ 2 J →L[ℝ] Hperp at R\n  change (∀ g : Lp ℝ 2 J, (R g : Lp ℝ 2 J)=g-P g) at hR\n  change (∀ g : Lp ℝ 2 J,\n    B.adjoint g=HP0.subtypeL (B0.adjoint (R g))) at hAmbient\n  change (∀ f : Lp ℝ 2 J, (∫ z, f z ∂J)=0 →\n    ∃ fP : HP0,\n      HP0.subtypeL fP=condExpL2 ℝ ℝ (μ:=J) measurable_snd.comap_le f ∧\n      let fperp : Hperp := R f\n      let fV : HP0 := V0.adjoint fperp\n      B.adjoint (fperp : Lp ℝ 2 J)=HP0.subtypeL (ΓP0 fV) ∧\n      HP0.subtypeL (ΓP0 fV)=ΓP (HP0.subtypeL fV) ∧\n      ‖f‖^2=‖fP‖^2+‖fperp‖^2 ∧ ‖fV‖≤‖fperp‖) at hGlobal\n",
          "detail": "Literal compiled BODY span;exact preceding locals remain in scope.",
          "lean_source_region": {
            "path": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ActualRootCommutation.lean",
            "source_raw_sha256": "8567673eba335e7c1209f8bd90ce510954426bd5bbcdef6ff53ea97889762748",
